    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48-a4">

                <pb facs="0208" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg124"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moule to Mr.
                            Lord</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hangchow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 3,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: Last evening I met, informally, all
                    the American missionaries at present in Hangchow to confer on the recent action
                    of the mandarins, of which you will, no doubt, receive detailed accounts from
                    Mr. Houston and others, in suddenly arresting certain
                    Chinese who have been engaged in selling or mortgaging<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d48-f1"/> land to foreign missionaries.</p>
                <p>We are unanimous in thinking the case a most serious one; and, although it is
                    possible that one single mission has, inadvertently, specially excited the
                    hostility of the mandarins, the arrests, which have either been made or
                    threatened, include persons who have sold property to all or nearly all of the
                    others.</p>
                <p>For our own (the C. M. S.) mission I propose to make a representation to the
                    British consul as soon as I have explicit information of the actual arrest of
                    persons who have sold property to us.</p>
                <p>Meantime, as it is thought desirable that you should be assured of our unanimity
                    in viewing the present emergency as critical for us all, I have asked Mr.
                        Houston to be good enough to inclose these few lines
                    with his communication to you.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE E. MOULE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">C. M.
                            S</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—The only mission in connection with which I hear of proscriptions is
                        Mr. McCarthy’s. I believe he has purchased no
                        property.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d48-f1" n="*" xml:id="d48-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Lord thinks “leasing” would be a better word to convey
                    the idea intended to be conveyed.— F.F.L.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
